+## Ordered Down implementation package, 2026-09-28
+
+`WP-DOWN-ORDERED-20260928` implements `DOWN-DECODE-ORDERED-CONSUMER-v1`.
+The originating product constraint is cold P40000 Prefill latency with no
+accuracy loss. Its downward budget is the measured 17.56-second Down family;
+value returns through the current whole-core API, reporting Decode jointly.
+The incumbent is the 50f7323 source / installed 0.8.1 persistent Down path.
+
+The initial composition decodes canonical packed nibbles with the incumbent
+Marlin transformed scale bytes, permutes K32 groups into the two existing
+accumulation chains, runs two FP32-output tensor products and merges them with
+explicit FP32 add/scale and BF16-before-residual rounding. It retains one
+layer's BF16 weights, one at-most-8000-row permuted activation panel and two
+FP32 partial outputs in dead GDN scratch (784,465,920 bytes, plus the existing
+2,883,584-byte tail reservation). Only aligned prefixes of at least 8,000 rows
+select this large-M dataflow; smaller prefixes and padded tails retain the
+declared incumbent before enqueue. This boundary is fixed before timing. No arena
+growth or persistent all-layer decoded weights are allowed. The K permutation
+and producer/read/merge costs belong to the complete candidate timing.
+
+Numerical admission begins with the fixed-shape incumbent comparator, all
+FP4 codes and transformed-scale cases; real-weight checks pin four Down layers
+chosen before timings by scale distribution. Preserve complete output equality
+on identical inputs, scale bits, finite checks and actual-row tails. A changed
+reduction or numerical tolerance is forbidden. A first failure permits only
+one causally justified correction. Compile/debug fixes that do not change the
+dataflow do not constitute a parameter search.
+
+The first admissible complete candidate returns to short, 8K and 40K real API
+direction checks. Maximum two dataflow variants and 30 minutes of real-model
+GPU process time before compose/reject; no additional profiling campaign.
+Any component performance screen uses checkpoint weights, a frozen panel,
+same-ELF mirrored incumbent/candidate comparisons and includes all conversion
+costs. A negative complete direction closes this version. A positive direction
+requires affected full-range numerical/API/resource/release qualification
+before default selection. Raw files stay in `.q3x-work/down-ordered-20260928/`.
